those four multiboard add/remove hooks are no longer needed.
Both UIs read the live state directly:
StatsUI.j: udg_CompanionUnit[], udg_CompanionCount, udg_TamedUnit
StatsLiteUI.j: same live companion/pet globals, refreshed by timer
So the old GUI triggers are not needed to make StatsUI/StatsLiteUI show companions or pets.
But I would not delete them yet. There are still direct JASS references:
[QuestGiver.j (line 329)](H:/Pelit/PotS_JASS/QuestsAndDialogs/QuestGiver.j:329) calls MultiboardUpdate_Add_Companion
[QuestGiver.j (line 435)](H:/Pelit/PotS_JASS/QuestsAndDialogs/QuestGiver.j:435) calls MultiboardUpdate_Remove_Companion
[Pet.j (line 613)](H:/Pelit/PotS_JASS/Companions/Pet.j:613) calls MultiboardUpdate_Add_Tamed
[Pet.j (line 490)](H:/Pelit/PotS_JASS/Companions/Pet.j:490) and [Pet.j (line 790)](H:/Pelit/PotS_JASS/Companions/Pet.j:790) call MultiboardUpdate_Remove_Tamed
You can disable the old multiboard GUI triggers in-map if the goal is to stop using the old visual multiboard. Keep the trigger objects present for now so existing gg_trg_... references still compile. The clean follow-up is to remove those direct TriggerExecute(...) calls from QuestGiver.j and Pet.j, then the four hook triggers can be deleted safely.
Also note: UnitExperience3.j still calls old multiboard level-update triggers, but StatsUI/StatsLiteUI do not need those either because they refresh level from the units directly.